# Kernel .config fragment for linux-meson-s7d-mainline-current
# 
# INSTRUCTION: Do NOT hand-edit this file. Instead:
#   1. Build once with: KERNEL_CONFIGURE=yes BOARD=odroidc5-mainline
#   2. In the menuconfig dialog, enable S7D-relevant Kconfig symbols:
#      - CONFIG_ARM_PSCI_FW=y
#      - CONFIG_ARM_GIC=y
#      - CONFIG_GIC_V3=y (if applicable)
#      - CONFIG_SERIAL_AMBA_PL011=y (UART)
#      - CONFIG_MMC=y, CONFIG_MMC_SDHCI=y (mainline stub)
#      - CONFIG_USB=y, CONFIG_USB_XHCI_PLATFORM=y (if S7D DTS improves)
#      - CONFIG_NET_STMMAC=y (Ethernet driver)
#      - CONFIG_DRM=y, CONFIG_DRM_MESON=y (HDMI, once mainline support lands)
#   3. After config, the full .config is saved in:
#      ~/.armbian/cache/linux-*-meson-s7d-mainline/...config
#   4. Copy that full .config here as-is (do not hand-trim).
#      The build system will use this as the baseline for next builds.
#
# STATUS: Skeleton — will be populated by first successful KERNEL_CONFIGURE=yes run.
